                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ederson de Souza",
                        "email": "ederson.desouza@intel.com",
                        "username": "edersondisouza"
                    },
                    "message": "That's a nice question! I'd love to have some way to add Zephyr support on CI here instead of downstream, as it would be perfect to catch issues early - even being able to just compile some test should be helpful (but some run on qemu would be even better).\nI'm not very familiar with CI here - other than it seems Jenkins based. It should be doable to build a Zephyr test application - Zephyr has some docker images (https://hub.docker.com/u/zephyrprojectrtos) that could be helpful. Any ideas?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ederson de Souza",
                        "email": "ederson.desouza@intel.com",
                        "username": "edersondisouza"
                    },
                    "message": "Done"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Andrew Jeffery",
                        "email": "andrew@codeconstruct.com.au",
                        "username": "amboar"
                    },
                    "message": "Done"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Andrew Jeffery",
                        "email": "andrew@codeconstruct.com.au",
                        "username": "amboar"
                    },
                    "message": "I don't yet have any that I'd be happy to run with in CI.\n\nI think for now I'll consider this for merging, with the expectation that you'll eventually find things that break your use-case with zephyr and we can then decide how to address them."
                },
                {
                    "file": "include/libpldm/compiler.h",
                    "line": 55,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Andrew Jeffery",
                        "email": "andrew@codeconstruct.com.au",
                        "username": "amboar"
                    },
                    "message": "Perhaps:\n\n```suggestion\n#ifndef EUCLEAN\n#define EUCLEAN 117\n#endif```\n\nThat could also resolve the dependence on the `__ZEPHYR` condition? We could add a comment about zephyr support."
                },
                {
                    "file": "include/libpldm/compiler.h",
                    "line": 55,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ederson de Souza",
                        "email": "ederson.desouza@intel.com",
                        "username": "edersondisouza"
                    },
                    "message": "Done"
                },
                {
